                    :operator {:type :variable :name '+}\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/assignments.md:274:                                        :ref {:type :variable :name 'x}}\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/assignments.md:277:                :ref {:type :variable :name 'x}}}}\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/assignments.md:321:                            :operator {:type :variable :name '+}\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/assignments.md:322:                            :operands [{:type :variable :name 'x_0}\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/assignments.md:327:                                  :operator {:type :variable :name '*}\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/assignments.md:328:                                  :operands [{:type :variable :name 'x_1}\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/assignments.md:330:               :body {:type :variable :name 'x_2}}}}\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/assignments.md:442:  {:type :variable-or-store\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/assignments.md:493:                               :operator {:type :variable :name '+}\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/assignments.md:499:                                      :operator {:type :variable :name '+}\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast_quickref.md:32:{:type :variable :name 'x}\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/assignment_strategies.md:177:                :operator {:type :variable :name '+}\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:207:{:type :variable\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:220:{:type :variable\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:227:{:type :variable\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:298: :body {:type :variable :name 'x}}\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:375: :operator {:type :variable :name '+}\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:384: :operator {:type :lambda :params ['x] :body {:type :variable :name 'x}}\n  1813\t## §10 Acceptance blockers and open items\n  1814\t\n  1815\t1. **Type-preserving canonical encoding in `dao.jing`** — declared,\n  1816\t   inherited, and **blocking every identity and deduplication use**\n  1817\t   (§4.2). `order-normalize` (`jing.cljc:45-64`) coerces every sequential\n  1818\t   value to a vector and `pr-str` drops metadata, so lists, seqs, and\n  1819\t   metadata-bearing vectors collide with plain vectors. No restricted\n  1820\t   value domain is claimed; the round-2 list-rejection rule is withdrawn\n  1821\t   as unsound. Rows, vectors, ledger-record maps, row\n  1822\t   deduplication, DAG sharing, process-local caches, content resolution by\n  1823\t   address, and ledger rows are all blocked alike until `dao.jing`'s\n  1824\t   encoding passes the conformance pairs of §4.2. This design does not\n  1825\t   close the item.\n  1826\t2. **The store-key domain is the `data` domain** (§2.2): every validator,\n  1827\t   extraction query, and store-slice encoding must use that one\n  1828\t   definition. This document now states it uniformly; the implementation\n  1829\t   phase must not reintroduce a narrower one, and the corpus must contain\n  1830\t   a numeric key beside the keyword one.\n  1831\t3. **Complete occurrence identity** (§2.5, §5.3, §8.4) — design work\n  1832\t   with stated mechanisms, not yet implementable. Source origins\n  1833\t   `[:source medium batch j]` must be supplied to the lowering and\n  1834\t   recorded in instruction provenance and initial expansion events;\n  1835\t   nested expansion events must carry both the declared-ref parent link\n  1836\t   and the parent record address, and the record must be minted after\n  1837\t   the parent's. The medium identity coordinate is whatever the\n  1838\t   composition names its program medium by; this document does not fix\n  1839\t   its shape, and that shape must be fixed before an origin can be\n  1840\t   written. The expander incarnation (§8.4.1) is a composition-minted\n  1841\t   random token, never a log-allocated id or a stream position; its\n  1842\t   uniqueness is the composition's warranty, discharged by the token's\n  1843\t   randomness, and no transactor is claimed to provide it. The\n  1844\t   `:incarnation` field of `ctx` and the token-minting step at\n  1845\t   construction are additions to `yin.vm.macro.md`'s `ctx` and expander\n  1846\t   construction that this document cannot make there.\n  1847\t4. **Macro batch and admission preservation** (§8.5) — design work with\n  1848\t   stated mechanisms. The ordered batch, the admission-order harvest\n  1849\t   catalogue of occurrence groups, the derived macro-only declaration\n  1850\t   catalogue, its admission validation, the validate-before-strip rule,\n  1851\t   and the adapter's path-and-entity tracking during inlining must exist\n  1852\t   before any tuple program containing a macro definition can be\n  1853\t   admitted. The legacy datom-batch contract is\n  1854\t   preserved only through the adapter-derived catalogue; tuple-native\n  1855\t   frontends operate\n  1856\t   under the separate declaration-order contract stated there. The v2\n  1857\t   expander itself does not exist yet (`src/cljc/yin/vm/` has no\n  1858\t   `macro.cljc`) and is not a blocker for tuple evaluation without\n  1859\t   macros; §8.4's event shape is specified against `yin.vm.macro.md`, not\n  1860\t   against code.\n  1861\t5. **Conservative dependency completion** (§7.7.2, §7.7.3) — design\n  1862\t   work with stated mechanisms. Global name discharge requires searching the\n  1863\t   store slice by key or resolving via primitive/module profiles (§7.7.2);\n  1864\t   convergence is over work items and all dependency facts, with the\n  1865\t   positional-environment context abstraction for values. Neither analysis exists in code;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
